---

import Layout from "../Layout/Layout.astro";
import InLine from "../Components/InLine.astro";

const citations = [
    {
        Inline: "1",
        mla: "Smart, Benjamin D et al. “Transgender women of color in the U.S. South: A qualitative study of social determinants of health and healthcare perspectives.” International journal of transgender health vol. 23,1-2 164-177. 17 Dec. 2020, doi:10.1080/26895269.2020.1848691",
    },
    {
        Inline: "2",
        mla: "James, Sandy E., et al. The Report of the 2015 U.S. Transgender Survey. National Center for Transgender Equality, Dec. 2016.",
    },
    {
        Inline: "3",
        mla: "CDC. “U.S. Uninsured Rate Drops by 15% since 2020.” NCHS Pressroom, 25 June 2025, www.cdc.gov/nchs/pressroom/releases/20250624.html. Accessed 4 Feb. 2026.",
    },
    {
        Inline: "4",
        mla: "Moaton, Tatyana . “San Francisco Community Health Center.” San Francisco Community Health Center, 2025, www.sfcommunityhealth.org/gamc-policy-brief-2025.\n",
    },
    {
        Inline: "5",
        mla: "Yılmaz, Büşra et al. “Transgender Individuals in the Eyes of Dental Professionals: A Data-Driven Study.” Oral diseases vol. 31,8 (2025): 2652-2660. doi:10.1111/odi.15310\n",
    },
    {
        Inline: "6",
        mla: "Johnson, Austin H et al. “Common barriers to healthcare for transgender people in the U.S. Southeast.” International journal of transgender health vol. 21,1 70-78. 11 Dec. 2019, doi:10.1080/15532739.2019.1700203",
    },
    {
      Inline: "7",
      mla: "James, Sandy E., et al. The Report of the 2022 U.S. Transgender Survey. National Center for Transgender Equality, Dec. 2022.",
    }

]
---

<Layout title="Facts" Citations={citations}>
    <div class="u-container flex flex-col content-center">
        <div class="flex flex-col z-2 w-full pt-40 pb-10 text-center">
            <h1 class="font-black text-4xl py-5" data-sy-reveal="chars">
                Facts
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="flex flex-col z-2 w-full pb-10 text-center">
            <h1 class="font-medium text-xl py-5 px-10" data-sy-reveal="lines">
                What we have set out to prove is that the issue of lack of healthcare access created in the American South affects transgender people negatively,
                in terms of both physical and mental health. We also have set out to prove that lack of access to certain treatments in health care is an
                intentionally created issue that targets transgender people.
            </h1>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 sm:grid-cols-1 z-2 text-center"  >

            <a href={"#source1"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[0].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title text-base-300">High Cost of care</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 font-bold grid-cols-1 text-xl/5">"Many avoided necessary care"</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Due to the challenges faced within the medical system,
                            many trans people choose to forego primary care.</div>
                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source2"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[1].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title text-base-300">Percentage of trans people uninsured</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">14%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">The discrimination faced by trans people within the healthcare
                            system makes it so that 14% are uninsured, unlike the 8.2% average.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source4"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[3].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title text-base-300">Georgia's spending</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">4.1 Million</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Many states spend more in litigation cost attempting to
                            deny trans people healthcare then they would giving those people healthcare ($10,000 in Georgia).</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source5"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[4].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300"></div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">19/20 Dentists</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Agreed that there was a social prejudice against trans people.
                            14.8% were aware of this social prejudice, and admitted that they held this social prejudice.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source6"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[5].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title text-base-300">Trans patients are often</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1  text-xl/5">Harassed and Misgendered</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">When they go to doctor's offices.
                            Additionally, many doctors lack knowledge on trans patients.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title text-base-300">Out to their providers</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">50%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Only about 50% of trans people
                            are open about being transgender to their medical providers.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Trans people who did not see a doctor because of cost</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">28%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Trans people who are uninsured, or their
                            insurance does not cover transition, are left to cover the cost themselves.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Didn't see a doctor because of fear of harassment</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">24%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Doctor's offices are not the
                            safe spaces that they should be for trans people.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Had a negative experience with healthcare within 1 year</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">47%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">The most common negative experiences were misgendering
                            and having to inform doctors about trans health.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Were denied treatment without a reason given</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">22%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Of those who were denied treatment, many
                            are never given a reason, and are left without the resources to find care.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Had a negative experience with health insurance within 1 year</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">26%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Common experiences included denial of transition related care,
                            refusal to change recognized gender, and denial of surgery coverage.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
            <a href={"#source7"} data-sy-reveal="words" title={"Source: " + citations[6].Inline}>
                <div class="hover-3d w-full h-full p-2" >
                    <figure class="max-w-100 rounded-2xl bg-blue-300 place-content-center">
                        <div class="stat">
                            <div class="stat-title whitespace-break-spaces text-base-300">Does not have access to transition related provider</div>
                            <div class="font-bold grid-cols-1 whitespace-nowrap text-2xl">43%</div>
                            <div class="font-light text-base-300 py-1">Many trans people do not have access to a medical provider
                            who specializes in trans people.</div>

                        </div>
                    </figure>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                    <div></div>
                </div>
            </a>
        </div>
        <div class="pt-8 z-4 flex flex-col px-24 text-center" >
            <p class="text-2xl font-bold">Explanations</p>
            <div class="px-85 flex flex-col">
                <span class="h-1 rounded-xl bg-neutral-800"></span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="py-8">
            <ul class="timeline timeline-snap-icon max-md:timeline-compact timeline-vertical">
                <li>
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source1">Source #1</time>
                        <a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8986221/#S0001" target="_blank">
                            <div class="text-lg font-black leading-none pb-2 flex flex-row items-center">Transgender women of color in the U.S. South: A qualitative study of social determinants of health and healthcare perspectives <div class="h-max">⇗</div></div>
                        </a>
                        In-depth interview with transgender women of color in the south, gives a look into what sorts of abuses and harms they face in their day to day lives, ranging from 20 topics including anything from emotional burden of healthcare interactions to the high cost of healthcare.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        No conflict of interest, approved by an official review board (Wake Forest School of Medicine Institutional Review Board), used approved methods for collection of data and had numerous experienced researches including from the department of social services and health.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        It gives a more personal look into how all these statistics about harms for trans people manifest in their day to day life, serving as more of an anecdotal piece of evidence than data and numbers.
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-end md:mb-10">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source2">Source #2</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black">2015 U.S. Transgender Survey</div>
                        A study which surveyed many trans people within the U.S.
                        Provides statistics of the 14% of all transgender people who are uninsured as well as the reasons for not seeing healthcare personnel.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        This is a survey conducted on over 27,000 trans people. They are all Self identified and anonymous online. More information can be found on their website <a href="https://transequality.org/"><span class="text-blue-800 underline">here.</span></a>
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        Demonstrates a general trend within the trans population, which shows not only a trend within the south, but the rest of the U.S. as well.
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source3">source #3</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black">U.S. Uninsured Rate Drops by 15% since 2020</div>
                        A press release by the CDC which demonstrates the uninsured rate on June 25th, 2025.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        Published by the CDC, which attempts to report unbiased data for the benefit of the public.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        This shows the usual average rate of uninsurance, which is quite small in comparison to the transgender rate.
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-end md:mb-10">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source4">source #4</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black">San Francisco Community Health Center</div>
                        A policy brief meant for policy makers. Demonstrates the amount spent to deny trans people healthcare.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        SF Community Health Center is a credible/federally qualified organization, and the papers they cite are also credible sources.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        Shows how pervasive this issue is, compares the US to other countries who are similar democracies and developed, as well as pointing out the harms for both the people and the paradoxical economic harms for the states that have these healthcare preventing policies.
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source5">Source #5</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black leading-none">Transgender Individuals in the Eyes of Dental Professionals: A Data-Driven Study.</div>
                        A study done on dentists in the U.S. which proves a social prejudice against trans people.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        Methods and materials are published along with the study itself.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        For our factual premise to be true, we must prove that this issue is caused by a purposeful exclusion of trans people. A study like this helps to prove that by demonstrating that many are aware of the issue, but actively choose to continue.
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-end md:mb-10">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source6">Source #6</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black leading-none">Common barriers to healthcare for transgender people in the U.S. Southeast</div>
                        A study of the issues which arise when trans people do seek healthcare. Provides a secondary reason as to why the healthcare provided to trans people is lacking.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        No conflict of interest, conducted by experienced researchers and methods/research approved by the IRB at Kenyon College.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        Provides for good anecdotal evidence, looks into transgender experience and treatment when they attempt to seek out healthcare (i.e. misgendering, doctors not being trained well to deal with transgender patients, hostile providers)
                    </div>
                    <hr />
                </li>
                <li>
                    <hr />
                    <div class="timeline-middle">
                        <svg
                                xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
                                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                                fill="currentColor"
                                class="h-5 w-5"
                        >
                            <path
                                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.857-9.809a.75.75 0 00-1.214-.882l-3.483 4.79-1.88-1.88a.75.75 0 10-1.06 1.061l2.5 2.5a.75.75 0 001.137-.089l4-5.5z"
                                    clip-rule="evenodd"
                            />
                        </svg>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-start mb-10 md:text-end">
                        <time class="font-mono italic scroll-m-40" id="source7">Source #7</time>
                        <div class="text-lg font-black">The Report of the 2022 U.S. Transgender Survey</div>
                        An updated version of the 2015 U.S. Transgender survey. Surveyed many trans people within the U.S.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">Why is this source credible?</div>
                        The survey was conducted on 84,000 trans adults & 8,000 trans youths.
                        <div class="spacer" />
                        <div class="text-lg font-bold">How does it prove our factual premise?</div>
                        Demonstrates the change in statistic between the past 7 years. Demonstrates that this is a continued problem.
                    </div>
                </li>

            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>